Lab 8: Implement Canary Releases Using OpenShift Service Mesh
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Deploy new versions of applications alongside existing versions using OpenShift Service Mesh
Configure traffic splitting between stable and canary versions of an application
Implement progressive traffic routing strategies for canary releases
Monitor application health and performance during canary deployments
Execute rollback procedures when canary versions fail health checks
Understand the benefits and best practices of canary release patterns
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, deployments)
Familiarity with OpenShift CLI (oc) commands
Knowledge of YAML configuration files
Understanding of microservices architecture principles
Basic networking concepts and HTTP traffic routing
Experience with command-line interfaces
