Why This Matters
Canary releases are crucial for modern application deployment because they:

Reduce Risk: By exposing only a small percentage of users to new versions initially, you minimize the impact of potential issues
Enable Data-Driven Decisions: Real-world performance data helps determine whether to proceed with or rollback deployments
Improve User Experience: Users experience fewer disruptions as problems are caught early with limited exposure
Support Continuous Delivery: Teams can deploy more frequently with confidence, knowing they can quickly rollback if needed
